PUBLIC DEMONSTRATION DATA

The local demonstration is built from pinned public datasets and deterministic
synthetic commerce records. Source revisions and checksums are recorded in
ops/demo/data/sources.lock.json.

| Dataset | Material used | Terms |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Amazon Shopping Queries Dataset (ESCI) | Product metadata and query-product judgments | Apache-2.0 |
| Shopping Queries Image Dataset (SQID) | Product-to-image URL index | MIT metadata |
| Amazon Berkeley Objects (ABO) | Listing metadata and product images | CC BY 4.0 |
| DZShip | Algerian wilaya and commune reference data | MIT |

ESCI is available from https://github.com/amazon-science/esci-data. SQID is
available from https://huggingface.co/datasets/crossingminds/shopping-queries-image-dataset.
ABO and its license are available from
https://amazon-berkeley-objects.s3.amazonaws.com/index.html. DZShip is
available from https://github.com/DZBuild-com/dzship.

The normalized CSV manifests are repository data, not production exports.
Downloaded source images and optimized copies remain outside Git. ABO images
retain their CC BY 4.0 terms. Product imagery reached through the SQID URL index
is not relicensed under the AGPL or MIT metadata license; anyone hosting or
redistributing those images remains responsible for the applicable image
rights. Synthetic names, contacts, orders, shipments, events, costs, messages,
and operational records do not represent real people or transactions.

Demo release media images include optimized copies of these catalog images.
They have been resized and converted to WebP. The bundled image manifest maps
each copy to its source; MEDIA-SHA256SUMS identifies the packaged files.
